Subject: Restore Exynos local domain hardware after a failed power-off

The failed DPU0 off sequence can change the PMU power request and time out
before the status bits reach OFF. The generic power domain correctly
remains active after proposal0043, so its normal unwind does not call
power-on for that domain. Restore the local hardware using the existing
power-on and saved-register sequence before returning the original error.

--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/cal-if/pmucal_local.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/cal-if/pmucal_local.c
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
  */
 int pmucal_local_disable(unsigned int pd_id)
 {
-	int ret, i;
+	int ret, restore_ret, i;
 
 	exynos_ss_pmu(pd_id, __func__, ESS_FLAG_IN);
 
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@
 							pmucal_pd_list[pd_id].save[i].offset,
 							pmucal_pd_list[pd_id].save[i].value);
 		}
+		/* The failed sequence may already have changed the power request. */
+		restore_ret = pmucal_local_enable(pd_id);
+		if (restore_ret)
+			pr_err("%s %s: failed to recover pd(%u): %d\n",
+			       PMUCAL_PREFIX, __func__, pd_id, restore_ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
